## Status

Self-excluded: **no verified public benchmark numbers** were found for the exact model/ID `gpt-5.2-codex` / `openai/gpt-5.2-codex` in accessible sources at time of research.

## Research notes

- Accessible metadata (not benchmark scores): Artificial Analysis lists GPT-5.2 Codex (Xhigh) as a proprietary OpenAI reasoning model (released December 2025, deprecated in AA view with suggestion to consider GPT-5.3 Codex), supporting text/image input and text output, with 400k-token context window, knowledge cutoff Aug 31 2025, and pricing around $1.75/$14.00 per 1M tokens (cache discount 90%) in AA snapshots. OpenRouter lists `openai/gpt-5.2-codex` with provider routing and supported parameters.
- OpenAI's "Introducing GPT-5.2-Codex" announcement describes capability improvements and states state-of-the-art performance on SWE-Bench Pro and Terminal-Bench 2.0, but the accessible fetched text did not provide extractable numeric benchmark scores for this exact model/ID (results were presented in non-extractable form in the fetched content).
- Artificial Analysis reported Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates as unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot; no standalone verified numeric benchmark scores for this exact model/ID were found in accessible sources.
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

